.TH Test-HomebridgeLocationGeneration 1 "December 2025" "docker-homebridge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Test-HomebridgeLocationGeneration \- Automated test for Homebridge location-based artifact and certificate generation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Test-HomebridgeLocationGeneration
[\fB--test-location\fR <location>] [\fB--help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Automated test suite that validates the New-LocationConfig script by comparing generated artifacts against baseline reference files. The test performs the following validations:
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies existence of generated files (compose file, env file, certificates directory)
.IP \(bu 2
Compares generated Docker Compose file against baseline
.IP \(bu 2
Compares generated environment file against baseline
.IP \(bu 2
Compares certificate request configuration against baseline
.IP \(bu 2
Performs field-by-field comparison of certificate signing request (CSR)
.IP \(bu 2
Performs field-by-field comparison of public key certificate
.PP
The test generates artifacts by calling:
.RS
.nf
build/New-LocationConfig --env-file=test/homebridge-<location>.env
make New-HomebridgeCertificates LOCATION=<location>
.fi
.RE
.PP
Upon successful completion of all tests, generated artifacts are automatically cleaned up. If any test fails, artifacts are left in place for inspection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --test-location <location>
Location name to test (default: fake-wa). The test will use test/homebridge-<location>.env as the environment file.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH FILE STRUCTURE
.SS Baseline files (expected):
.TP
test/baseline/homebridge-<location>.yaml
Baseline Docker Compose file
.TP
test/baseline/homebridge-<location>.env
Baseline environment file
.TP
test/baseline/homebridge.config/<location>/certificates/
Baseline certificate directory containing certificate-request.conf, self-signed.csr, and public-key.pem
.SS Generated files (actual):
.TP
homebridge-<location>.yaml
Generated Docker Compose file
.TP
homebridge-<location>.env
Generated environment file
.TP
homebridge.config/<location>/certificates/
Generated certificate directory
.SH USAGE
.SS Run test with default location (fake-wa):
.RS
.nf
\fB./test/Test-HomebridgeLocationGeneration\fR
.fi
.RE
.SS Run test with specific location:
.RS
.nf
\fB./test/Test-HomebridgeLocationGeneration --test-location=us-wa\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The script reports the number of passed tests vs total tests. If all tests pass, it exits with status 0 after cleaning up generated files. If any test fails, artifacts remain for inspection.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B Required:
diff, openssl, awk, sed
.TP
.B Scripts:
build/New-LocationConfig, build/Declare-BashScript
.TP
.B Make targets:
New-HomebridgeCertificates
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR New-LocationConfig (1),
.BR openssl (1),
.BR diff (1)
